# Unit 11: Profile Visibility & Share Functionality

## Goal

Add the ability for users to toggle their profile visibility and easily copy their public shareable link from the dashboard.

## Design

- Follow `ui-context.md`
- Clean toggle switch in the Profile section
- Prominent "Copy Share Link" button that shows the full public URL
- Success feedback when link is copied
- Link only works when `is_public = true`

## Implementation

### 1. Service Update
- Add to `src/services/profiles.service.ts`:
  - `toggleProfileVisibility(userId: string, isPublic: boolean)`

### 2. UI Updates
- In Profile page (`app/dashboard/profile/page.tsx`):
  - Add visibility toggle (use shadcn Switch if available, or simple button)
  - Show current public URL (e.g. `https://yoursite.com/profile/john-doe-abc123`)
  - "Copy Link" button with clipboard functionality

### 3. Integration
- Update Public Profile page to respect `is_public` flag properly
- Add visibility status indicator in dashboard

## Dependencies

- None new (or shadcn Switch component if needed)

## Verify when done

- [ ] User can toggle profile between private and public
- [ ] Public URL is correctly generated and displayed
- [ ] Copy link button works (copies full URL to clipboard)
- [ ] Public profile page correctly shows 404/private message when `is_public = false`
- [ ] Changes persist and work after refresh
- [ ] Matches UI Context
- [ ] `npm run build` succeeds
- Update `progress-tracker.md` and mark Unit 11 complete

**Important Constraints:**
- Keep it simple — no advanced sharing options
- Auto-generate slug if not already done
- No social share buttons yet